":\"https://bestanimalnames.com/about/\"},\"publisher\":{\"@type\":\"Organization\",\"name\":\"BestAnimalNames\",\"url\":\"https://bestanimalnames.com\"},\"mainEntityOfPage\":{\"@type\":\"WebPage\",\"@id\":\"https://bestanimalnames.com/blog/animal-names-from-different-cultures/\"},\"wordCount\":153,\"articleBody\":\" The world speaks thousands of languages, each with its own beautiful naming traditions. Drawing from world cultures gives your pet a name rich with meaning, history, and global perspective. Japanese Animal Names <strong>Kuma</strong> (bear), <strong>Tora</strong> (tiger), <strong>Sakura</strong> (cherry blossom), <strong>Yuki</strong> (snow), <strong>Sora</strong> (sky), <strong>Ryu</strong> (dragon), <strong>Hoshi</strong> (star), <strong>Mochi</strong>, <strong>Sushi</strong>. African & Swahili Names <strong>Simba</strong> (lion), <strong>Zuri</strong> (beautiful), <strong>Jabari</strong> (brave), <strong>Amani</strong> (peace), <strong>Safari</strong> (journey), <strong>Nala</strong> (gift), <strong>Kito</strong> (precious jewel). Celtic & Gaelic Names <strong>Finn</strong>, <strong>Niamh</strong>, <strong>Aoife</strong>, <strong>Cian</strong>, <strong>Oisin</strong>, <strong>Brigid</strong>, <strong>Rowan</strong>, <strong>Lugh</strong>, <strong>Morrigan</strong>. Nordic & Scandinavian Names <strong>Freya</strong>, <strong>Loki</strong>, <strong>Odin</strong>, <strong>Thor</strong>, <strong>Sven</strong>, <strong>Astrid</strong>, <strong>Bjorn</strong>, <strong>Sigrid</strong>, <strong>Fenrir</strong>. Sanskrit & Indian Names <strong>Bodhi</strong>, <strong>Kali</strong>, <strong>Shanti</strong>, <strong>Devi</strong>, <strong>Ravi</strong>, <strong>Priya</strong>, <strong>Asha</strong>, <strong>Indra</strong>, <strong>Raj</strong>. Native American Names Explore our name generators for {antechinus}, {alligator-gar}, {aldabra-giant-tortoise}, {african-civet}, and {arabian-wolf} to find the perfect name for your companion. <strong>Dakota</strong>, <strong>Cheyenne</strong>, <strong>Winona</strong>, <strong>Kiona</strong>, <strong>Nokomis</strong>, <strong>Takoda</strong>, <strong>Paco</strong>, <strong>Mika</strong>. Discover more naming ideas: {sandhill-crane}, {peterbald}, {zebra-moray}, {caribbean-flamingo}, {canary}, and hundreds more animal name generators.\",\"image\":\"https://bestanimalnames.com/images/og/blog-animal-names-from-different-cultures.png\",\"inLanguage\":\"en\"}14:[[\"$\",\"script\",null,{\"type\":\"application/ld+json\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"$1d\"}}],[\"$\",\"script\",null,{\"type\":\"application/ld+json\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"{\\\"@context\\\":\\\"https://schema.org\\\",\\\"@type\\\":\\\"FAQPage\\\",\\\"mainEntity\\\":[{\\\"@type\\\":\\\"Question\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"Is cultural appropriation a concern with pet names?\\\",\\\"acceptedAnswer\\\":{\\\"@type\\\":\\\"Answer\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Using names from other cultures with respect and appreciation is generally fine. Learn the meaning and pronunciation to honor the source.\\\"}},{\\\"@type\\\":\\\"Question\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"What's the most popular global pet name?\\\",\\\"acceptedAnswer\\\":{\\\"@type\\\":\\\"Answer\\\",\\\"text\\\":\\\"Simba (Swahili) and Luna (Latin) are among the most popular culturally-derived pet names worldwide.\\\"}}]}\"}}],\"$L1e\",\"$L1f\",\"$L20\"]\n1e:[\"$\",\"script\",null,{\"type\":\"application/ld+json\",\"dangerouslySetInnerHTML\":{\"__html\":\"{\\\"@context\\\":\\\"https://schema.org\\\",\\\"@type\\\":\\\"BreadcrumbList\\\",\\\"itemListElement\\\":[{\\\"@type\\\":\\\"ListItem\\\",\\\"position\\\":1,\\\"name\\\":\\\"Home\\\",\\\"item\\\":\\\"https://bestanimalnames.com/\\\"},{\\\"@type\\\":\\\"ListItem\\\",\\\"position\\\":2,\\\"name\\\":\\\"Blog\\\",\\\"item\\\":\\\"https://bestanimalnames.com/blog/\\\"},{\\\"@type\\\":\\\"ListItem\\\",\\\"position\\\":3,\\\"name\\\":\\\"Animal Names from Different Cultures: 200+ Global Ideas 🌏\\\",\\\"item\\\":\\\"https://best